{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe `data_resource` class of the terraform-config-inspect corroborator can never return a match\nagainst the real audited binary. `declaration_present` on `data.aws_ami.base` abstains\n`no_unique_address` even when the data resource is present in the module.\n\nFound while root-causing `widish-chemic-goitered` (`f95d-19f6-7e58-4a8e`). It is a separate\nmechanism from that ticket's schema skew and is deliberately NOT bundled into it: that one is a\npriority-1 CI blocker whose fix must stay minimal, while this is a correctness gap that blocks\nnobody. Filing it so it is not lost.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe real tool keys its `data_resources` map by the FULL address including the `data.` prefix.\nGround truth from the pinned binary\n(`github.com/hashicorp/terraform-config-inspect@2fb54c236733ee65ee877105d595c124c993c64d`) on a\nmodule containing `data \"aws_ami\" \"base\" {}`:\n\n```\n/data_resources/data.aws_ami.base/...\n```\n\n`_subject_class_name` at `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py:186-187` strips that\nprefix:\n\n```python\nif len(parts) == 3 and parts[0] == \"data\":\n    return \"data_resource\", \".\".join(parts[1:])\n```\n\nso `_match` looks up `aws_ami.base` in a map keyed `data.aws_ami.base` and misses at\n`src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py:390-392`, abstaining `no_unique_address`.\n\nThe unit suite does not catch it because the hand-written fake payload in `_fixture_binary` keys\nits `data_resources` entry `aws_ami.base`, matching the stripped form rather than the tool. The\ntest and the code agree with each other and both disagree with the tool. Reproduced directly: with\nthe schema and directory-argument fixes from `widish-chemic-goitered` applied in a throwaway\nharness against the real binary, `variable.region` and `module.vpc` both MATCH while\n`data.aws_ami.base` abstains `no_unique_address`.\n\n## Approach\n\nLook data resources up under the address the tool actually emits, and make the fake stop\ncontradicting it. Keep accepting the `data.<type>.<name>` subject form callers already write —\nonly the lookup key changes — so no caller has to be updated.\n\nRebasing the fake payload on one captured real document is the point of the change, not a side\neffect: the fake diverging from the tool is what hid this bug and the schema skew both.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py` — key the `data_resource` lookup on the full\n  `data.<type>.<name>` address.\n- `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py` — key the fake payload's `data_resources`\n  entry the way the tool does, and add a negative case pinning that a stripped key does NOT match.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED: with the real binary on `PATH`, assert `declaration_present` on `data.aws_ami.base`\n  abstains `no_unique_address` before the fix.\n- GREEN: the same call returns a match after it, and the existing\n  `test_exact_declaration_matches_every_supported_class[data.aws_ami.base-data_resource]`\n  parametrization still passes against the corrected fake.\n- Failure path: a genuinely absent data resource (`data.aws_ami.missing`) still abstains\n  `no_unique_address`, so the fix does not turn the lookup into a wildcard.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [non-codebase] Against the real audited binary, `corroborate_diagnostic(..., \"declaration_present\",\n      \"data.aws_ami.base\")` on a module declaring that data resource returns outcome `match`;\n      recorded as a ticket comment with the pre-fix `no_unique_address` result beside it.\n- [x] `data.aws_ami.missing` still abstains `no_unique_address` against the same module.\n- [x] The fake payload's `data_resources` key is the full `data.<type>.<name>` address; verified\n      by `pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py -q` being green with the\n      existing data-resource parametrization unchanged.\n- [x] `make verify` is green before the change is pushed to Gerrit.\n\n## Completion evidence\n\nGerrit change 2735 merged as 2abea9dd884e83607170aac7c62fed002a0a1d07. Local `make verify` passed. RED/GREEN oracle: `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_data_resource_lookup.py` failed before the production change and passed after it; `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py` fake payload now uses the full `data.aws_ami.base` key.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788754604005037001,"uuid":"26dfbcdc-80af-4164-9bd9-f21663f3dbbf"}